@startuml
' Revision: ax removal (2026-10-27).
title Current launch routes and target one-shot path
actor "Caller / operator" as caller
participant "curator-run\ncaller identity" as launcher
participant "curator env resolve\ncaller-side subprocess" as curator
participant "agents-management\nin-process library" as spawn
participant "Native provider\ncaller-side child" as native
participant "Selected session-manager plugin\nhosted process / session owner" as manager
participant "swarma-dispatcher\nservice UID unspecified" as dispatcher
participant "swarma-user-launcher\nroot" as root
participant "curator-run exec\nagent UID worker-<label>" as agent
participant "credential broker\nservice UID unspecified" as broker
participant "Harness\nagent-side process" as harness
participant "user-manager helper\nroot" as helper
participant "Session host\nconfigured service principal" as targethost
participant "Workspace executors\napproved child UID / dispatcher workspace contract" as workspaceexec
participant "Board change requests\norchestrator" as changes
participant "swarma-session-runner\napproved agent-side executor" as targetrunner

== CURRENT interactive API: SPEC 0.5.1-draft ==
caller -> launcher : curator-run <env-id> ...
launcher -> launcher : static help / version return first: no config discovery or read\notherwise discover config locations, normalize / validate argv, then all-location retired-policy existence guard and active config read
alt invalid config, retired ax.json entry or usage
  launcher --> caller : terminal refusal; no resolve / launch
else accepted invocation
  launcher -> curator : env resolve <canonical env-id> --repair --format json
  curator -> curator : resolve / repair persistent managed home (Curator-owned)
  curator --> launcher : closed fragment v1 / v2 / v3 / v4
  launcher -> launcher : map environment; defaults / host / permissions\nhosted: resume, stdin and terminal gates before build
  alt resolve / mapping / defaults / host / permission refused
    launcher --> caller : SPEC 6 refusal; no child / receiver
  else hosted resume (non-new intent)
    launcher -> manager : resume delegated request; no caller-side plan build,\nprovider-limit, network or composition step
    manager --> launcher : operation outcome / readable session record
    launcher --> caller : result or typed refusal; no native fallback
  else gates admit (new launch)
    launcher -> spawn : BuildLaunchWithEnvironment(..., LaunchModeInteractive)
    spawn --> launcher : admitted plan value or refusal (no child)
    alt plan admission refused
      launcher --> caller : plan_refused; no provider-limit / network / launch step
    else plan admitted
      launcher -> launcher : explicit providerlimits.AvailabilityFor\noptional native network admission; compose values
    alt provider-limit / network / composition refused
      launcher --> caller : plan_refused / plan_provider_limited / network refusal\nno retry, weaker posture or model substitution
    else composed launch
      alt hosted selected - registered and selected conforming manager
        launcher -> manager : new delegated launch, profile / digest request\nFRONT-DOOR 3-5 / 5.8
        manager -> manager : compose admitted provider launch; own process / session
        manager --> launcher : operation outcome / readable session record
        opt attached launch
          launcher -> manager : attach with private terminal fd3 / status fd4
          manager --> launcher : terminal exchange / result
        end
        launcher --> caller : result or typed refusal; no native fallback
      else native route
        launcher -> launcher : immediately before launch: binary check, Codex MCP stat,\nprompt probe / PrepareLaunch; first failure refuses
        alt late check refused
          launcher --> caller : exec_provider_missing / mcp_layer_* / sysprompt_*\nno provider starts
        else late checks admitted
          launcher -> native : start composed Binary / argv / full env / cwd / exact stdin
          launcher -> native : terminal foreground / signal forwarding / stop-continue
          native --> launcher : child exit or signal
          launcher --> caller : restore terminal; child exit / 128 + signal
        end
      end
    end
    end
  end
end
note over launcher
  [[../SPEC.md#4-composition-algorithm SPEC 4]] / [[../SPEC.md#46-hand-off-and-exec SPEC 4.6]] / [[../SPEC.md#49-hosted-payload-and-receiver-handoff SPEC 4.9]] / [[../SPEC.md#6-errors-and-diagnostics SPEC 6]].
  Launcher owns invocation state, operation journals and liveness; the manager owns hosted processes.
  Direct wait / terminal behavior:
  [[../README.md#environment-and-transport README Environment and transport]].
  FRONT-DOOR 3-5 / 5.8: selected manager takes delegated launch.
  Auto without a registered/selected manager: native + one-line notice.
  Explicit hosted instead refuses session_host_missing with reason (after earlier checks).
  Exact-plan activation and real Muse hosting remain gated; native executes the child directly.
  Missing Codex layer: deliberate new invocation lets Curator repair; launcher never repairs it.
end note

== TARGET one-shot: NOT IMPLEMENTED; dispatcher Slice 0 local headless only ==
caller -> caller : resolve / compose plan; select credential source; digest PATH / profile / harness / B / manifest / write scope / resources\nexec identity / body digest come from protected dispatcher prepare, not caller selection
caller -> dispatcher : Unix-socket client; composed plan; no secret material
alt size / authority / grants / capacity or Slice 0 combination refused
  dispatcher --> caller : terminal refusal before provisioning
else admitted request
  dispatcher -> dispatcher : prepare: resolve protected exec-policy relation; refuse caller outside bound\npin identity / body digest in input/1; start / retry / recovery refuse policy drift
  dispatcher -> dispatcher : provision account / broker binding; claim execution\ndistinct effect IDs; retries reuse each operation's ID
  dispatcher -> workspaceexec : swarma-workspace-materialize before work\nrelay admitted base archive; journal digest; no dispatcher repository
  workspaceexec -> workspaceexec : verify archive paths / kind-mode / content against immutable B manifest\nmissing / extra / mismatch refuses before work\nstandalone repo / fresh config / no hooks or remotes; read-only resources
  dispatcher -> root : closed privileged stdin request; approved executor
  alt generation / ownership / executor digest / exec-policy drift or qualification / duplicate receipt refused
    root --> dispatcher : typed refusal; no second start
  else privileged checks admit
    root -> root : apply pinned exec profile / verify body digest before child code\nclass / qualified host / admission checks remain\nuser-manager lifecycle; bounded staging; atomic receipt before UID drop
    root -> agent : execute approved curator-run under agent UID\ncaller-owned 0-2 and read-only FD3; no internal handles
    agent -> agent : bounded read once; verify admitted digest and values\nresolve protected credential_binding locally\ncheck harness surfaces by digest or root-owned surfaces\nprovider proxy only; provider-side search off without trusted-circle opt-in
    alt bad intake / unknown contract / digest / drift / source or binding refused
      agent --> dispatcher : terminal refusal evidence (transport unpublished)
    else selected qualified broker channel
      agent -> broker : fresh peer-authenticated lease; correlation launch_id = digest
      broker -> broker : active ledger (uid,generation), binding, grants / caller chain,\nprofile / harness / channel / endpoint / binary / policy checks
      alt broker unreachable / revoked / mismatched / unqualified
        broker --> agent : typed refusal
        agent --> dispatcher : no native-login / alternate-source fallback
      else qualified lease
        broker --> agent : leased material; execution channel only
        agent -> agent : recheck destination binding immediately before execution
        alt destination recheck refused
          agent --> dispatcher : terminal binding refusal; no harness
        else destination binding still admits
          agent -> harness : execute verified plan; Claude token via qualified env channel
          note over agent,harness
          Slice 0 Claude setup-token has no refresh.
          Expiry / auth failure requires re-enrollment and restart.
          Later Codex: executor/runner renews (8 s deadline); broker alone refreshes.
          Receipt transport and ownership across exec: unspecified in spec 10.4;
          no assumed post-exit emitter or surviving renewal loop.
          end note
        end
      end
    end
  end
  opt round end / cancellation / max-runtime stop
    dispatcher -> helper : exec.stop for owned generation / execution
    helper -> helper : verify latest receipt authority; completed stop replays without signals\nuser-manager spec 4.4 / 4.7 single stop / retirement scope\nall UID processes: TERM / grace / KILL; stop per-user service domain\naccount-wide quiet absence, escaped descendants included
    alt absence confirmed
      helper --> dispatcher : termination receipt
    else processes remain / evidence unknown
      helper --> dispatcher : processes_remain / unknown evidence
      dispatcher -> dispatcher : no capacity release or replacement
    end
  end
  opt workspace round ended and account-wide absence confirmed
    dispatcher -> dispatcher : workplace write fence where applicable; further round tool calls refused
    dispatcher -> workspaceexec : swarma-workspace-export; fixed environment / no network
    workspaceexec -> workspaceexec : no link following / skip Git administration; compare mode AND content\nmode-only / equal-blob file-symlink modify; deletion prior mode\ncaps / unsafe paths / collisions / special files refuse whole export
    alt export recorded
      workspaceexec --> dispatcher : change set / digests; dispatcher draft result fields (SPEC 10.5)
      dispatcher --> caller : workspace-result/1 design label; original caller principal only
      caller -> changes : board accepts resource; deterministic import requested
      changes -> changes : bounded canonical-manifest recomputation from repository immutable B, never plan\nrefuse if base_commit != B or manifest_digest differs; retain admission checks
      changes -> changes : scratch-index B plus mode-aware change set -> signed C\nhooks / filters / drivers disabled
      changes -> changes : present exact-C diffs / blobs as inert read-only resources by digest\noutside harness discovery roots; qualified strict adapter before discovery-capable tree entry
      changes -> changes : explicit review-role / class / placement admission; distinct from producer\nreviews exactly C; flagged hunks acknowledged with no preceding automatic load\ncode runs only in R-VERIFY; acceptance does not admit control surfaces
      changes -> changes : findings -> rework on C; accepted exact head -> signed fast-forward\nmoved base -> refresh / re-review
    else export refused / unknown
      dispatcher -> dispatcher : retain export cleanup obligation; no home deletion without operator waiver
    end
  end
  opt cleanup effects confirmed and export recorded or operator-waived for workspace allocation
    dispatcher -> dispatcher : unbind THEN retire, each confirmed separately\nquiesce / declared-key cleanup then home deletion\nseparate revocation only for registered one-shot identity after retirement
  end
end
== TARGET session-host lifecycle: DISABLED until joint publication / qualification ==
caller -> dispatcher : owner-admitted start; session lifecycle authorisation may permit successors\nmember format unpublished
dispatcher -> dispatcher : durable session-scoped host admission permit for one logical_session_id
targethost -> targethost : durable session intent; closed delivery fence
targethost -> dispatcher : host_start in dispatch-op/1\nlogical_session_id / execution_id / controller_epoch / op_id
dispatcher -> dispatcher : configured session-host principal only; execution under permit\nsuccessor requires lifecycle authorisation / previous-claim confirmed absence\nidempotent per (logical_session_id, op_id)\nper-physical-start (execution_id, controller_epoch, op_id) claim / fence / receipt
alt cancellation / fence change before physical call
  dispatcher -> dispatcher : prevent stale call or reconcile; no authority widening
else admitted start
  dispatcher -> root : approved runner via existing claim / effect / root-receipt path
  alt ambiguous physical call
    dispatcher -> dispatcher : resolve same effect / receipt; never launch twice\nstop through exec.stop if required
  else runner started
    root -> targetrunner : approved executor under agent UID; user-manager lifecycle
    targetrunner -> targethost : fresh authenticated channel\ncurrent-epoch registration and readiness before delivery
  end
end
opt permitted host-requested stop
  targethost -> dispatcher : host_stop in dispatch-op/1; execution under permit
  dispatcher -> dispatcher : configured host principal only; journaled E-stop\nhost-requested, distinct from owner cancel; no start authority
  dispatcher -> helper : exec.stop; same single termination scope
  helper --> dispatcher : confirmed account-wide absence or processes_remain / unknown
end
note over targethost,dispatcher
  Host failure retains claim and closed fence until reconciliation.
  Transport, session permit / authorisation, host_stop and fence/cancel/crash ordering need joint publication (SPEC 10.5).
  Controller-only re-adoption keeps execution_id; replacement uses a new one.
  Fresh runner checks the native session lock; only dispatcher invokes root.
end note
note over caller,helper
  [[../SPEC.md#101-immutable-input-descriptor-transport-and-limits SPEC 10.1]] / [[../SPEC.md#102-caller-dispatcher-privileged-launcher-and-executor SPEC 10.2]] / [[../SPEC.md#103-broker-binding-credential-delivery-and-rollout SPEC 10.3]] / [[../SPEC.md#104-signals-stop-receipts-and-cleanup SPEC 10.4]] / [[../SPEC.md#105-typed-refusals-exit-status-and-activation-questions SPEC 10.5]].
  Initial service uses broker connection / framing rules; recovery / readiness before admission.
  Absent / unready service refuses; queue / events / long waits later on same transport.
  FD3 mechanism joint publication gates activation with intake / digest / framing / read deadline.
  Prefer completely staged bounded immutable bytes; pipe needs capacity / feeder / deadline / cleanup.
  R-TRANSFER workspace export precedes retirement; recorded export or operator waiver before deletion.
  Separate retirement metadata export: service-generated closed schema only.
  Separate operator home retention has no confidentiality guarantee.
  Start receipt is not readiness. Exit is not proof of process absence / cleanup.
  Broker owns persistent binding / credential store; root launcher owns atomic start receipt.
  Dispatcher owns durable claims, outcomes and supervision: Unix-socket service from first slice.
  Process fate table / replaced-daemon writer fence: user-manager spec 7 (R-FATE); no live supervisor adoption.
  Cross-account workspace: standalone repository; private .git / common directory / refs / index / fresh config; no hooks.
  No inherited .git backlink / executable local config / credential helpers; copy / reflink preserves rule.
  Linked worktrees only within one account; shared objects immutable / read-only; formats open (SPEC 10.5).
  R-TIME: authenticated / operator-controlled installer time source; durable dispatcher / broker watermark.
  Expiry max(now, watermark); not_before min(now, watermark); no untrusted advance; operator reset.
  Expiry-driven home / binding destruction also requires boot-inclusive monotonic elapsed lifetime.
  Exact intake envelope / invocation, consumed-plan receipt, numeric exits and signal encoding: unspecified in spec 10.1 / 10.4 / 10.5.
  No interactive FD3/FD4 reuse; no board dependency; SH2 host lifecycle / donor B remain disabled pending publication.
end note
note over caller,helper
  Launch obligations - SPEC 10.1-10.2 / 10.5-10.6
  R-TRANSFER: plan digest covers B / mode-aware manifest digest / write scope / pinned exec-profile identity and body digest.
  Manifest from immutable B: path / Git kind-mode / content identity; archive exact-match before work.
  Export compares mode and content: mode-only / equal-blob file-symlink modify; deletion prior mode.
  Board import recomputes canonical manifest from repository B, never plan; base_commit / manifest_digest must match.
  R-EXEC selection: protected machine policy beside R-NETBIND; profile-lock / placement / class bound.
  Dispatcher pins at prepare; launch / retry / recovery use pin; out-of-bound request or drift refuses.
  Launcher verifies policy body digest before any child code; existing class / host / qualification checks remain.
  R-NET-TOOL: read-only task resources covered by digest; bound provider proxy only.
  No web by default; plan disables provider-side search, invisible to network rules.
  Only operator-granted trusted-circle opt-in: qualified server search or platform Unix-socket web service.
  R-STANDING: verify settings / hooks / MCP / instructions by digest before exec, or root-owned surfaces.
  Drift refuses (code unpublished); repair is explicit re-materialization.
  Plan / root-owned surfaces alone do not exclude ambient candidate discovery (SPEC 10.2).
  R-STANDING: host loop requires trusted class AND local agent placement; circle membership is insufficient.
  Remote identities receive workplaces only; donor-side loops; circle does not change placement.
  Optional local-only reviewer / requester-exclusion policies remain unchosen and off (SPEC 9).
  OPEN requirement (SPEC 9): bridge / helper / dispatcher, stage A, jointly publish ingress / relay /
  start / quiesce / export / reconnect lifetime and generation-bound process-creation fence.
  Full fix with stage A contract package; no mechanism selected or normative change shown.
  R-EXEC: qualify full invocation / env / transitive interpreted code-config inputs; inert inspection only.
  Protected entrypoints / config, disabled or pinned code loading; executable allowlist alone is insufficient.
  Negative scripts / inline eval / imports / plugins / startup-env injection / direct-indirect heavy bypass; inert positive controls.
  D-PATH wrapper ownership / fixed subcommand alone is insufficient; unprovable local tool goes to R-VERIFY.
  User manager owns OS exec allowlist; R-VERIFY builds / tests / code execution on another machine.
  R-UNTRUSTED refused in Slice 0 / user-manager v0; workplace zero egress / donor-side loop.
  Admission: R-CEILINGS / R-WATCH / R-ALLSTOP / R-RANGE-DENY / R-SOCKETS / R-SHARED (SPEC 10.6).
  Exact plan / transfer / opt-in formats and qualification remain open; no implementation claimed.
end note
note right of changes
  R-TRANSFER review - SPEC 10.2
  Explicit review-role grant: trusted-class local agent placement or person admitted to role;
  outside untrusted class and distinct from producer; circle alone grants no role / placement.
  Exact-C diffs / blobs first: inert read-only resources by digest, outside harness discovery roots.
  Candidate instructions / hooks / MCP / permissions / skills / executable discovery remain data.
  No automatic adoption at startup / reload / nested discovery / resume / child entry,
  before or after acknowledgement; record shows no preceding load; every flagged hunk acknowledged.
  Discovery-capable tree entry requires a qualified strict-context adapter before launch.
  Qualification covers hook / MCP / instruction / skill on each real harness tool path; none loaded / executed.
  Root-owned surfaces alone do not exclude ambient discovery. No qualification claimed.
  Acceptance is not control-surface admission; separate CIP-0002 admission required.
  Semantic prompt injection remains a review residual.
end note
@enduml
